.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "ModuleImporter"
.PP
by \fRNicholas C\&. Zakas\fP

.PP
If you find this useful, please consider supporting my work with a \fRdonation\fP\&.
.SH "Description"
.PP
A utility for seamlessly importing modules in Node\&.js regardless if they are CommonJS or ESM format\&. Under the hood, this uses \fRimport()\fP and relies on Node\&.js's CommonJS compatibility to work correctly\&. This ensures that the correct locations and formats are used for CommonJS so you can call one method and not worry about any compatibility issues\&.

.PP
The problem with the default \fRimport()\fP is that it always resolves relative to the file location in which it is called\&. If you want to resolve from a different location, you need to jump through a few hoops to achieve that\&. This package makes it easy to both resolve and import modules from any directory\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.SS "Node\&.js"
Install using \fRnpm\fP or \fRyarn\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @humanwhocodes/module\-importer

# or

yarn add @humanwhocodes/module\-importer
.fi
.PP

.PP
Import into your Node\&.js project:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// CommonJS
const { ModuleImporter } = require("@humanwhocodes/module\-importer");

// ESM
import { ModuleImporter } from "@humanwhocodes/module\-importer";
.fi
.PP
.SS "Bun"
Install using this command:

.PP
.PP
.nf
bun add @humanwhocodes/module\-importer
.fi
.PP

.PP
Import into your Bun project:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { ModuleImporter } from "@humanwhocodes/module\-importer";
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
After importing, create a new instance of \fRModuleImporter\fP to start emitting events:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// cwd can be omitted to use process\&.cwd()
const importer = new ModuleImporter(cwd);

// you can resolve the location of any package
const location = importer\&.resolve("\&./some\-file\&.cjs");

// you can also import directly
const module = importer\&.import("\&./some\-file\&.cjs");
.fi
.PP

.PP
For both \fRresolve()\fP and \fRimport()\fP, you can pass in package names and filenames\&.
